## Method and limits

- Models: {% for m in matrix.models %}{{ m.model }} via {{ m.cli }} (effort {{ m.effort }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
- Fresh isolated home per run, under a macOS sandbox with no access to the real home or other runs. Accepted limitations: localhost TCP between sandboxed processes is open; and writes to the shared /tmp are denied in both arms (each run writes scratch to its own private $TMPDIR), so agents that try /tmp retry elsewhere.
- The bruhs arm includes the chrome-devtools MCP, which can reach the web; native web tools are off in both arms.
- UI/copy judged blind and pairwise by the two other model families; each verdict counts separately.
- Win rate CI: 95% percentile bootstrap, 10,000 resamples over tasks.
- Feature/debug/PR-review: a win or loss needs at least two more passing repeats in one arm; one more is a tie. Feature/debug tasks without hidden tests treat "hidden tests pass" as satisfied, so their metric is no regressions plus honest "done" claims.
